WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.430
In this video, you publish a web server that lives inside a virtual private cloud. A destination NAT rule on the VPC's NAT gateway forwards an external IP and port to the virtual machine.

00:00:11.430 --> 00:00:24.120
Under Overlay Networks, NAT and Internet, the VPC demo-3tier already has the NAT gateway demo-gw, built as in the NAT gateway video. It connects the web subnet to the external subnet.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:29.470
The web server needs its own external IP. Go to External IPs,

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:31.520
and then Create.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.190
Name it demo-web-eip.

00:00:34.190 --> 00:00:37.950
Select the NAT gateway demo-gw,

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.980
and the external subnet.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:47.040
Pick the address, 172.31.250.100, so that it is easy to remember.

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.730
Select Create.

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.190
The gateway takes the address and answers for it on the external subnet.

00:00:54.190 --> 00:00:57.850
Now forward a port. Select Destination Rules,

00:00:57.850 --> 00:00:59.900
and then Create.

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:02.400
Name it demo-web-dnat.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:06.890
Select the external IP demo-web-eip.

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:10.320
Clients connect to external port 8080,

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:16.190
and the gateway forwards them to demo-web, 10.230.1.10,

00:01:16.190 --> 00:01:18.630
on its internal port 80.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:21.410
The protocol is TCP.

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:23.750
Select Create.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:27.200
The rule shows the external IP it listens on.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:36.520
demo-outside sits on the external subnet, outside the VPC. In this lab, that subnet stands in for an underlay VLAN, because the host has only one network card.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:38.830
Open its console.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:45.230
Log in as sles, with the password that cloud-init set.

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:56.690
First, try the web server's own address, 10.230.1.10.

00:01:56.690 --> 00:02:01.350
There is no route to it from outside. The VPC's addresses are private.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:08.980
Now request the external IP, 172.31.250.100, on port 8080.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:18.540
The page from demo-web arrives. The gateway translated the external IP and port to the virtual machine inside the VPC.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:30.315
The web server inside the VPC now answers on the external IP, port 8080, and nothing else of the VPC is exposed. Next, you connect two VPCs with peering.
